        <headline>Coastal Flood Advisory issued September 24 at 8:35PM EDT until September 25 at 11:00AM EDT by NWS Newport/Morehead City NC</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Up to 1 to 2 feet of inundation above ground level is
possible in low-lying areas near shorelines and tidal
waterways resulting in a low threat of property damage along
the Neuse River. Some roads and low lying property including
parking lots, parks, lawns, and homes adjacent to the
waterfront will experience shallow flooding.

* WHERE...Areas along the Pamlico Sound, Trent, Bay and lower
Neuse Rivers, and adjacent tidal creeks.

* WHEN...Until 11 AM EDT Friday.

* IMPACTS...Flooding of lots, parks, and roads with only
isolated road closures expected.
</description>
        <instruction>If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be
closed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of
unknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone
property.</instruction>
